"""Kaggle runner: zero-training VALIDATION-only C2 decode + per-path estimators (dual T4).

Two things in one run, on the val-gen-ic validation subsample
(temporal_symbol_validation_v1, 24 np.linspace dates, 12,256 windows, val_data sha256
4cce31bc...19bf7):

  A. Small C2 (production model, segment 179, sha 4ee469d4...) validation predictions,
     decoded exactly like the C2 sealed-OOS kernel (kaggle_c2_18d_alpha_oos): model code
     at commit e4b92bb, from_pretrained(num_sectors=86, num_size_buckets=0,
     context_layer=6, use_size_percentile=True, size_mlp_hidden_dim=64),
     prod T0.65/p0.8/N5, seed 20260906, EFFECTIVE_BATCH 64.
  B. Every sampled path's terminal return close_d10/last_close-1 (+ window keys) for
     C2 N5 and Best@475 N5 (Beta v2.1 ModelScope release, sha e1bd5584...,
     EFFECTIVE_BATCH 256 as in the val-gen-ic kernel) and, if time allows,
     Best@475 N16 (T0.65/p0.8).

Order: C2 N5 -> Best@475 N5 -> (optional) Best@475 N16. Each phase = 2 workers with
dynamic in-order date claims; per-date shards land immediately; each arm is scored
(mean / median / trimmed mean / mean-excluding-max) the moment its last shard lands;
comparison.json (incl. pre-registered decision rules, C2/ours rank-blend grid and
style-shrink transform) is rewritten after every arm.

Never trains. Never mounts or reads the sealed OOS package (the only input dataset is
a val-only copy; the runner aborts if any evaluation_manifest.json is mounted).
"""

